// `@bits(n)` is a ruled NON-GOAL and was deleted: it never read its arguments, appeared in no SPEC text and
// in zero corpus files, yet set the "field is marked" flag, so it silently stood in for `@field`. A packing
// backend spends one bit on a `bool` inside its own `writeBool`; an author wanting bit-exact integers packs
// them into the smallest integer carrier in their own type.
@generate(Serializable, Deserializable)
type value R { @bits(3) int32 a; }
fn int32 main() { return 0; }
